+// The flight reads page 2 at least every kAruImuReadMs, PA keyed or not, and again with
+// page 0 in its 1 Hz sample (D-75). Page 2 holds no magnetometer data - statistics the
+// Nicla computed over its own windows - so the PA-off rule of the samples (D-45) does not
+// apply to it. Twice per second, not once: the ARU shows only its last completed window
+// and rebuilds its pages at 10 Hz on its own clock, so a 1 Hz read whose phase sits near
+// the window edge skips windows (host test imu_window_reads); at 500 ms a window goes by
+// unread only when the loop is held for more than ~400 ms.
+static const uint32_t kAruImuReadMs = 500;
